From 0b892fb7f781a2ed54a82270461ccd6c4b5d1584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mamam Kasir Dev <dev@mamamayam.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:27:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] style: adopt Leci reference app's navy brand color
 (#0A2540, replacing orange #FF6B2C)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Colors sampled directly from pixels in the user's Leci screenshots
(primary button fill, header title text). AppColors.brand is the single
source of truth for this across the app, so every screen using it
(primary buttons, header icons, badges, chips, etc.) picks up the new
navy automatically — no other files needed touching, confirmed no
hardcoded #FF6B2C remained anywhere.

Explicit exception per user decision: the dashboard hero sales card
keeps its existing dark gradient rather than becoming solid navy —
verified unchanged (still uses AppColors.heroGradient, not
AppColors.brand).

AppColors.info (#3B7DD9) already matched Leci's sampled chart/amount
blue exactly — no change needed there.
---
 lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart | 29 ++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart b/lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart
index 25b6550..d44a4d1 100644
--- a/lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart
+++ b/lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart
@@ -2,12 +2,12 @@ import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
 
